00:39:50,208 --> 00:39:51,537
It was insane.

1006
00:39:51,538 --> 00:39:53,437
When I see something great,

1007
00:39:53,438 --> 00:39:55,847
I want to turn it into my work.

1008
00:39:55,848 --> 00:39:57,407
So I thought, "What should I do?"

1009
00:39:57,408 --> 00:40:00,717
"How can I work with Kyung Rok?"

1010
00:40:00,718 --> 00:40:02,918
Then I ran into you in a pub.

1011
00:40:03,318 --> 00:40:06,057
So I decided to send you a highball.

1012
00:40:06,058 --> 00:40:07,257
(She plucked up the courage
and sent him a highball.)

1013
00:40:07,258 --> 00:40:09,787
- It was an honor. Seriously.
- So...

1014
00:40:09,788 --> 00:40:10,958
(Work with me.)

1015
00:40:11,188 --> 00:40:12,188
(You?)

1016
00:40:12,189 --> 00:40:13,197
(You're the best!)

1017
00:40:13,198 --> 00:40:14,258
You're something else.

1018
00:40:14,698 --> 00:40:16,328
- She's much younger.
- That's right.

1019
00:40:16,498 --> 00:40:17,628
We became close in no time.

1020
00:40:19,138 --> 00:40:22,168
Before I forget, I prepared...

1021
00:40:22,768 --> 00:40:24,767
- a small gift.
- A gift again?

1022
00:40:24,768 --> 00:40:27,107
- Nice.
- Kyung Rok, you go around...

1023
00:40:27,108 --> 00:40:28,237
- giving gifts.
- Seriously.

1024
00:40:28,238 --> 00:40:31,147
You should ride Rudolph,
not a motorcycle.

1025
00:40:31,148 --> 00:40:33,277
- Santa Claus.
- He really is Santa Claus.

1026
00:40:33,278 --> 00:40:34,348
Hongdae's Santa Claus.

1027
00:40:35,788 --> 00:40:36,888
- I'll open it.
- Okay.

1028
00:40:37,118 --> 00:40:39,857
They're my favorite accessories.

1029
00:40:39,858 --> 00:40:40,988
Is it a bracelet?

1030
00:40:41,318 --> 00:40:42,427
I brought the ones I used.

1031
00:40:42,428 --> 00:40:45,188
I bought it...

1032
00:40:45,288 --> 00:40:47,398
from a street stall.
It isn't expensive.

1033
00:40:48,328 --> 00:40:50,067
- It's like a pirate's item.
- Yes.

1034
00:40:50,068 --> 00:40:51,427
- It's like a musical item.
- Yes.

1035
00:40:51,428 --> 00:40:53,298
(The pirate's mark is a key point.)

1036
00:40:53,538 --> 00:40:54,867
- It's romantic.
- You know,

1037
00:40:54,868 --> 00:40:56,267
I'm going crazy right now.

1038
00:40:56,268 --> 00:40:58,938
Do you know what
my favorite Crying Nut song is?

1039
00:40:59,078 --> 00:41:00,208
"The Pirate’s Path."

1040
00:41:01,538 --> 00:41:04,107
- That necklace is fitting.
- It's so cool.

1041
00:41:04,108 --> 00:41:05,818
- It's fitting.
- That's right.

1042
00:41:06,018 --> 00:41:08,448
- You got the telepathic message.
- I know.

1043
00:41:09,148 --> 00:41:10,487
(Cheering)

1044
00:41:10,488 --> 00:41:12,017
- Look at this.
- You like it.

1045
00:41:12,018 --> 00:41:13,417
I love it. It's insane.

1046
00:41:13,418 --> 00:41:14,487
There's something else.

1047
00:41:14,488 --> 00:41:15,727
Is there something else?

1048
00:41:15,728 --> 00:41:19,398
I thought it'd be nice
to give you a classic.

1049
00:41:19,798 --> 00:41:21,197
She likes books.

1050
00:41:21,198 --> 00:41:22,467
- It's really fun.
- Is it fun?

1051
00:41:22,468 --> 00:41:23,997
- It's fun.
- On the flyleaf...

1052
00:41:23,998 --> 00:41:24,998
(She spots something.)

1053
00:41:26,098 --> 00:41:28,438
(The page is full
of the handwritten message.)

1054
00:41:28,668 --> 00:41:31,137
- What kind of a book is it?
- Classics always survive.

1055
00:41:31,138 --> 00:41:32,578
That's right. They never die.

1056
00:41:33,338 --> 00:41:35,178
- Let's become the classics.
- Okay.

1057
00:41:35,948 --> 00:41:38,077
It's such a cool saying.

1058
00:41:38,078 --> 00:41:39,218
It's a cool saying.

1059
00:41:40,018 --> 00:41:43,218
I have so many worries
about Kyung Rok Day.

1060
00:41:43,388 --> 00:41:45,318
- I wanted to ask you something.
- Okay.

1061
00:41:45,448 --> 00:41:48,358
Why don't you do
a collaborative performance...

1062
00:41:48,788 --> 00:41:50,258
