1063
00:41:50,858 --> 00:41:52,128
If we do that...

1064
00:41:52,728 --> 00:41:53,858
She feels honored as a fan.

1065
00:41:54,128 --> 00:41:55,627
It'll be a good opportunity.

1066
00:41:55,628 --> 00:41:56,767
I love the idea.

1067
00:41:56,768 --> 00:41:58,368
BIBI and Crying Nut.

1068
00:41:58,568 --> 00:41:59,737
(Oh, my!)

1069
00:41:59,738 --> 00:42:00,968
It's a unique combination.

1070
00:42:01,168 --> 00:42:02,568
Sing a rock version
of "Bam Yang Gang."

1071
00:42:03,208 --> 00:42:04,768
Red bean jelly with chestnut

1072
00:42:05,438 --> 00:42:07,908
Sing it like that.
The sweetest snack

1073
00:42:09,008 --> 00:42:10,247
It'll be interesting.

1074
00:42:10,248 --> 00:42:11,647
That's right. Red bean jelly
can be the drinking snack.

1075
00:42:11,648 --> 00:42:13,047
- It'll be nice.
- It's a good idea.

1076
00:42:13,048 --> 00:42:14,048
(End of the meeting)

1077
00:42:14,348 --> 00:42:16,348
- It'll be nice.
- Kyung Rok!

1078
00:42:16,818 --> 00:42:18,748
- It'll be nice.
- Kyung Rok!

1079
00:42:19,158 --> 00:42:20,618
Hey, Tigers!

1080
00:42:20,888 --> 00:42:22,357
Gosh, you're here.

1081
00:42:22,358 --> 00:42:23,588
- Hello.
- Hey.

1082
00:42:23,828 --> 00:42:25,688
- They're Far East Asian Tigers.
- Far East Asian Tigers.

1083
00:42:25,858 --> 00:42:28,628
- Why don't we go and say hello?
- Sure.

1084
00:42:28,798 --> 00:42:30,628
- Hello.
- Gosh.

1085
00:42:30,798 --> 00:42:34,438
The hottest indie rockstars
in Hongdae!

1086
00:42:34,538 --> 00:42:35,967
- You've been doing well, right?
- Of course.

1087
00:42:35,968 --> 00:42:37,967
Far East Asian Tigers?

1088
00:42:37,968 --> 00:42:39,677
- I'll introduce you to someone.
- They're hot these days.

1089
00:42:39,678 --> 00:42:41,308
Okay.

1090
00:42:42,278 --> 00:42:43,848
I'll introduce you to someone.

1091
00:42:44,478 --> 00:42:46,717
- This is BIBI. Hyeong Seo.
- Hello.

1092
00:42:46,718 --> 00:42:48,277
- Hello.
- And...

1093
00:42:48,278 --> 00:42:50,588
- this is Far East Asian Tigers.
- Right.

1094
00:42:50,618 --> 00:42:51,618
You know them, right?

1095
00:42:51,619 --> 00:42:53,588
We'll be performing together
on Kyung Rok Day.

1096
00:42:54,558 --> 00:42:55,618
It's an honor.

1097
00:42:55,858 --> 00:42:58,028
I wish you guys would
greet each other from now on.

1098
00:42:58,088 --> 00:42:59,098
- Right.
- That sounds great.

1099
00:42:59,628 --> 00:43:02,768
So that is how artists get together.

1100
00:43:03,298 --> 00:43:04,868
When I'm in Jebi Coffee House,

1101
00:43:05,168 --> 00:43:06,998
I meet a lot of bands that visit.

1102
00:43:07,868 --> 00:43:09,437
It feels like a salon of the past.

1103
00:43:09,438 --> 00:43:10,667
- Salon! Exactly.
- Right?

1104
00:43:10,668 --> 00:43:12,407
It's like a place
for Romantic painters of France.

1105
00:43:12,408 --> 00:43:13,408
- It has that feel.
- Right.

1106
00:43:13,409 --> 00:43:15,277
- Artists meet so naturally.
- Right.

1107
00:43:15,278 --> 00:43:16,747
New ideas could be created
through those encounters.

1108
00:43:16,748 --> 00:43:18,177
- It's a salon.
- It's a salon.

1109
00:43:18,178 --> 00:43:19,218
(Hongdae salon)

1110
00:43:19,548 --> 00:43:22,918
- Well, let's eat together sometime.
- Right.

1111
00:43:23,248 --> 00:43:24,248
I'll see you next time.

1112
00:43:24,249 --> 00:43:26,258
- Bye!
- Bye!

1113
00:43:26,688 --> 00:43:28,088
I'll mascot you.

1114
00:43:28,418 --> 00:43:29,627
- "Mascot?"
- Yes.

1115
00:43:29,628 --> 00:43:31,958
(He says goodbye to BIBI as well.)

1116
00:43:32,188 --> 00:43:33,998
Can the Soot Black Moomoo
Bald Head's show...

1117
00:43:34,428 --> 00:43:36,028
- be done in Jebi Coffee House?
- Do you have something prepared?

1118
00:43:36,398 --> 00:43:37,798
I have to hold the Bald Show soon.

1119
00:43:38,398 --> 00:43:40,538
Do this and shake off
your hair powder.

1120
00:43:40,698 --> 00:43:42,038
Like this?

1121
00:43:42,198 --> 00:43:43,708
People can see you from the top.

1122
00:43:44,438 --> 00:43:46,437
The ceiling is open.

1123
00:43:46,438 --> 00:43:48,408
When the lights are on from there,

1124
00:43:48,608 --> 00:43:49,708
it will shine very brightly.

1125
00:43:50,808 --> 00:43:51,977
That's when I'll spin my head.

1126
00:43:51,978 --> 00:43:54,018
(A fantastic performance
is expected.)

1127
00:43:54,548 --> 00:43:56,018
- Get back safely.
- Happy New Year.

1128
00:43:56,088 --> 00:43:57,088
(His bike has finally been fixed.)

1129
00:43:57,089 --> 00:43:58,317
- Happy New Year.
- Goodbye.

1130
00:43:58,318 --> 00:43:59,758
- Thank you.
- The sun has set already.

1131
00:44:00,218 --> 00:44:02,017
You must feel lonely
when you head back home.

1132
00:44:02,018 --> 00:44:03,057
Right.

1133
00:44:03,058 --> 00:44:04,127
That's how it would feel
after being in a loud place.

1134
00:44:04,128 --> 00:44:05,158
Right.

1135
00:44:07,698 --> 00:44:09,727
(Along with his favorite bike
that feels a lot smoother,)

1136
00:44:09,728 --> 00:44:12,028
(Kyung Rok heads back home.)

1137
00:44:13,838 --> 00:44:15,468
He has flowers by his chest.

1138
00:44:15,598 --> 00:44:18,637
The petals fall off if I carry them
with the handle of the motorcycle.

1139
00:44:18,638 --> 00:44:20,278
- You can't do that.
- Right. You can't do that.

1140
00:44:22,138 --> 00:44:24,678
(He returns home
after the sun is down.)

1141
00:44:26,018 --> 00:44:28,547
(Letting out a breath)

1142
00:44:28,548 --> 00:44:30,088
Gosh.

1143
00:44:31,948 --> 00:44:33,758
(Placing down)

1144
00:44:37,028 --> 00:44:40,458
(Letting out a breath)

1145
00:44:45,798 --> 00:44:48,498
(He had the rock spirit
worn around his neck.)

1146
00:44:49,638 --> 00:44:53,238
(He puts it back
after folding it nicely.)

1147
00:44:54,008 --> 00:44:56,848
The moment you take off
your bandana at home,

1148
00:44:57,178 --> 00:44:58,647
- you feel like a different person.
- Right.

1149
00:44:58,648 --> 00:45:00,247
Right? The off button?

1150
00:45:00,248 --> 00:45:01,418
Right. The off button.

1151
00:45:03,688 --> 00:45:06,818
(Switching on)

1152
00:45:08,088 --> 00:45:11,188
(He starts turning on the lights
around the house.)

1153
00:45:14,028 --> 00:45:16,097
(Unlike the bright day
filled with natural light,)

1154
00:45:16,098 --> 00:45:17,428
Done.

1155
00:45:17,528 --> 00:45:20,498
(the night in Kyung Rok's house
has become much calmer.)

1156
00:45:21,198 --> 00:45:22,398
Today's flowers.

1157
00:45:24,268 --> 00:45:27,308
(He heads to the kitchen with the
flowers he bought during the day.)

1158
00:45:29,378 --> 00:45:31,848
(Being careful)

1159
00:45:32,578 --> 00:45:33,618
Gosh.

1160
00:45:34,778 --> 00:45:36,018
They must've felt cold.

1161
00:45:38,018 --> 00:45:39,788
(Turning around)

1162
00:45:43,858 --> 00:45:47,158
(I should prune them.)

1163
00:45:49,198 --> 00:45:51,298
(Kyung Rok carefully prunes
the flowers...)

1164
00:45:52,638 --> 00:45:53,697
(he brought preciously.)

1165
00:45:53,698 --> 00:45:56,438
- He's very romantic.
- Right.

1166
00:45:58,838 --> 00:46:02,008
(The flower vases were put together
very quickly.)

1167
00:46:03,308 --> 00:46:04,878
(Placing down carefully)

1168
00:46:06,818 --> 00:46:10,318
(He places them
where he wanted to place them.)

1169
00:46:12,218 --> 00:46:13,888
(Fiddling)

1170
00:46:15,318 --> 00:46:16,357
(He opens the coffee beans
he bought today.)

1171
00:46:16,358 --> 00:46:18,388
- Coffee?
- Coffee!

1172
00:46:18,828 --> 00:46:20,428
(Sniffing)

1173
00:46:21,398 --> 00:46:24,868
(Yes. This is it.)

1174
00:46:28,668 --> 00:46:31,337
(He puts them into
the glass jars nicely...)

1175
00:46:31,338 --> 00:46:34,378
(and stores them in the cupboard.)

1176
00:46:37,548 --> 00:46:39,977
(He gets the blanket that has
dried up nicely in the sun.)

1177
00:46:39,978 --> 00:46:41,817
- It must've dried up nicely.
- Right.

1178
00:46:41,818 --> 00:46:43,218
(He gets the blanket that has
dried up nicely in the sun.)

1179
00:46:46,618 --> 00:46:48,988
(He opens the fridge.)

1180
00:46:49,788 --> 00:46:52,028
(Let's see.)

1181
00:46:53,058 --> 00:46:55,798
(Taking out a bunch of things)

1182
00:46:57,968 --> 00:47:02,238
(He heads to the kitchen with a lot
of things to prepare for dinner.)

1183
00:47:03,068 --> 00:47:04,868
(Thinking)

1184
00:47:06,308 --> 00:47:08,708
(He chooses a cup that he likes...)

1185
00:47:08,808 --> 00:47:09,808
(and adds in scorched rice.)

1186
00:47:09,809 --> 00:47:12,478
- Scorched rice?
- I crave some at night.

1187
00:47:12,608 --> 00:47:15,677
Since I won't be having a lot,
I use a cup.

1188
00:47:15,678 --> 00:47:17,787
It's bad to have a heavy meal
at night.

1189
00:47:17,788 --> 00:47:19,218
(He craves scorched rice at night
for a light meal.)

1190
00:47:19,858 --> 00:47:22,258
(As he spent a busy day,)

1191
00:47:23,658 --> 00:47:26,698
(he quickly prepares his dinner.)

1192
00:47:28,798 --> 00:47:30,998
(Shall I eat now?)

1193
00:47:33,368 --> 00:47:34,667
(His dinner...)

1194
00:47:34,668 --> 00:47:35,937
He orders food.

1195
00:47:35,938 --> 00:47:38,038
(looks a lot like his breakfast.)

1196
00:47:39,338 --> 00:47:41,438
(Mixing)

1197
00:47:43,478 --> 00:47:47,178
(He takes a bite
of the warm porridge first.)

1198
00:47:49,218 --> 00:47:51,748
(Chewing)

1199
00:47:58,588 --> 00:48:02,597
(Without any music playing,)

1200
00:48:02,598 --> 00:48:05,597
(the place is silent.)

1201
00:48:05,598 --> 00:48:06,868
It's really quiet.

1202
00:48:07,038 --> 00:48:08,668
- He became a different person.
- Right.

1203
00:48:09,038 --> 00:48:10,908
When I come back home,

1204
00:48:11,208 --> 00:48:14,478
it feels like
my house comforts me with a hug.

1205
00:48:14,638 --> 00:48:17,507
I tend to keep quiet...

1206
00:48:17,508 --> 00:48:19,048
and let myself recharge.

1207
00:48:21,448 --> 00:48:23,148
(Lifting)

1208
00:48:25,088 --> 00:48:27,118
(The scorched rice
has been soaked just right.)

1209
00:48:28,618 --> 00:48:29,628
(Slurping)

1210
00:48:30,188 --> 00:48:31,188
(Letting out a breath)

1211
00:48:32,258 --> 00:48:33,258
(Slurping)

1212
00:48:33,898 --> 00:48:34,928
(Letting out a breath)

1213
00:48:38,668 --> 00:48:43,268
(Just the sound of his spoon
and cup clashing can be heard.)

1214
00:48:44,208 --> 00:48:46,778
(Wiping)

1215
00:48:53,378 --> 00:48:54,548
After that...

1216
00:48:54,578 --> 00:48:58,317
(It was loud...)

1217
00:48:58,318 --> 00:49:02,158
(throughout the whole day.)

1218
00:49:04,828 --> 00:49:08,097
(The night deepens...)

1219
00:49:08,098 --> 00:49:10,468
(and I am alone.)

1220
00:49:11,968 --> 00:49:15,037
(It still doesn't...)

1221
00:49:15,038 --> 00:49:17,738
(feel so bad.)

1222
00:49:17,938 --> 00:49:19,978
When I was young,
there was no night or day.

1223
00:49:20,538 --> 00:49:23,548
I loved hanging out with friends
so much.

1224
00:49:23,708 --> 00:49:24,948
I drank during the day.

1225
00:49:25,108 --> 00:49:26,747
I drank for several days straight.

1226
00:49:26,748 --> 00:49:28,418
I even slept on the streets.

1227
00:49:28,748 --> 00:49:30,817
I freely enjoyed my life.

1228
00:49:30,818 --> 00:49:32,918
(The times I was carefree)

1229
00:49:33,058 --> 00:49:36,118
Now that those times have passed,

1230
00:49:36,428 --> 00:49:39,228
I feel like I need some time...

1231
00:49:39,528 --> 00:49:42,028
to talk with myself.

1232
00:49:42,698 --> 00:49:45,368
That is why
the time I spend alone...

1233
00:49:45,828 --> 00:49:47,098
has become a lot more precious.

1234
00:49:47,668 --> 00:49:50,608
I started enjoying
decorating the house...

1235
00:49:51,308 --> 00:49:53,008
and cleaning up the house.

1236
00:49:53,138 --> 00:49:55,737
I started working out
and taking care of myself.

1237
00:49:55,738 --> 00:49:56,847
(I am solely focused on myself now.)

1238
00:49:56,848 --> 00:50:00,178
I want to perform after writing
a song about my new self.

1239
00:50:00,678 --> 00:50:02,178
Of course,
"Speed Up Losers" is great,

1240
00:50:02,478 --> 00:50:03,888
but I want to sing about
my current emotions...

1241
00:50:04,488 --> 00:50:06,418
and this current generation.

1242
00:50:06,918 --> 00:50:08,018
I also want to be jumping around.

1243
00:50:08,558 --> 00:50:11,728
I don't want to look all mature
as a musician of 30 years.

1244
00:50:12,328 --> 00:50:13,897
I want to jump around...

1245
00:50:13,898 --> 00:50:15,798
- That's touching.
- as an active musician.

1246
00:50:16,028 --> 00:50:18,027
I don't want to fall behind
the musicians of this generation...

1247
00:50:18,028 --> 00:50:19,598
when it comes to energy.

1248
00:50:19,768 --> 00:50:21,668
I want to enjoy performing with them
as colleagues.

1249
00:50:22,298 --> 00:50:24,368
I want to give my energy
to the audience.

1250
00:50:24,568 --> 00:50:26,108
I want to make everyone jump.

1251
00:50:27,838 --> 00:50:29,177
I'm always progressing.

1252
00:50:29,178 --> 00:50:30,847
(Han Kyung Rock...)

1253
00:50:30,848 --> 00:50:33,548
(is still progressing.)

1254
00:50:34,618 --> 00:50:35,818
- Gosh!
- Gosh!

1255
00:50:36,418 --> 00:50:38,047
- That was great.
- Right.

1256
00:50:38,048 --> 00:50:39,957
- Thank you.
- The ending spoke right at me.

1257
00:50:39,958 --> 00:50:41,857
- Right. It was so touching.
- Right.

1258
00:50:41,858 --> 00:50:42,927
Right.

1259
00:50:42,928 --> 00:50:44,157
How was it for you?

1260
00:50:44,158 --> 00:50:46,957
You've been in Hongdae
for a while as well.

1261
00:50:46,958 --> 00:50:48,028
It really...

1262
00:50:48,658 --> 00:50:51,497
reminded me
of the times I was young.

1263
00:50:51,498 --> 00:50:55,638
I felt the emotions
that I loved and missed.

1264
00:50:56,168 --> 00:50:59,138
It was an admirable life.

1265
00:50:59,838 --> 00:51:03,548
You looked like an artist
who is devoted to the audience.

1266
00:51:04,078 --> 00:51:08,548
I witnessed the moments
of a fool for music.

1267
00:51:08,648 --> 00:51:12,388
A fool for music
is such a pleasant thing to hear.

1268
00:51:12,718 --> 00:51:15,988
I don't want myself
to become too clever.

1269
00:51:16,488 --> 00:51:18,457
- A fool for music.
- You sound like a poet.

1270
00:51:18,458 --> 00:51:20,427
- Gosh.
- That was so nice.

1271
00:51:20,428 --> 00:51:21,657
Gosh.

1272
00:51:21,658 --> 00:51:23,097
While seeing you today,

1273
00:51:23,098 --> 00:51:25,127
I thought that you looked
much younger than your age.

1274
00:51:25,128 --> 00:51:27,938
But I think your eyes
look the youngest.

1275
00:51:28,438 --> 00:51:30,908
You have the eyes of a young man.

1276
00:51:31,568 --> 00:51:33,638
Actually, I was reminded of Picasso.

1277
00:51:34,108 --> 00:51:37,708
- Picasso?
- Picasso once said this.

1278
00:51:37,808 --> 00:51:41,448
"It took me four years
to draw like Raphael,"

1279
00:51:42,018 --> 00:51:44,118
"but it took me my whole life
to draw like a child."

1280
00:51:44,818 --> 00:51:46,857
- Right.
- It's a really hard thing to do.

1281
00:51:46,858 --> 00:51:48,057
It's hard for us
to draw like a child...

1282
00:51:48,058 --> 00:51:50,888
because we adults know so much
and have experienced many things.

1283
00:51:50,928 --> 00:51:53,498
But I felt that through your eyes.

1284
00:51:53,628 --> 00:51:55,497
You have a sense of innocence
of a child.

1285
00:51:55,498 --> 00:51:56,898
That was why I thought
you never aged.

1286
00:51:57,068 --> 00:51:58,767
It was a day
that motivated me a lot.

1287
00:51:58,768 --> 00:52:01,098
That's such a great thing to hear.

1288
00:52:01,398 --> 00:52:02,967
It feels like we're in Hongdae
at 3am.

1289
00:52:02,968 --> 00:52:04,268
Gosh, this feels great.

1290
00:52:04,338 --> 00:52:05,838
All of us are drunk.

1291
00:52:07,138 --> 00:52:08,938
More peaches, please.

1292
00:52:09,748 --> 00:52:11,647
(The night in Hongdae never ends.)

1293
00:52:11,648 --> 00:52:12,648
(I Live Alone)

1294
00:52:12,848 --> 00:52:15,318
(Heave-Ho! Winter Survival)

1295
00:52:16,048 --> 00:52:17,817
(One, two)

1296
00:52:17,818 --> 00:52:19,888
- What? Running?
- Running?

1297
00:52:20,058 --> 00:52:21,258
Gosh!

1298
00:52:22,358 --> 00:52:24,088
I don't think it's a Fun Run,
judging by the speed.

1299
00:52:24,258 --> 00:52:25,588
It's not a Fun Run.

1300
00:52:25,828 --> 00:52:27,697
You could die during a Fun Run
at that speed.

1301
00:52:27,698 --> 00:52:30,098
I gained around 5kg
compared to the summer.

1302
00:52:30,498 --> 00:52:31,597
- Right now?
- Yes.

1303
00:52:31,598 --> 00:52:32,598
You look fine.

1304
00:52:32,599 --> 00:52:35,197
Since he's tall,
you can't tell if he gained 5kg.

1305
00:52:35,198 --> 00:52:37,007
My body felt a lot heavier.

1306
00:52:37,008 --> 00:52:38,968
That was why I decided
to lose some weight.

1307
00:52:39,778 --> 00:52:42,337
(He breathlessly runs somewhere.)

1308
00:52:42,338 --> 00:52:45,107
(Seoul Botanic Park)

1309
00:52:45,108 --> 00:52:46,818
- What?
- It's Seoul Botanic Park.

1310
00:52:47,848 --> 00:52:49,148
The Botanic Culture Center.

1311
00:52:50,018 --> 00:52:52,147
(He heads to the ticket booth
right away.)

1312
00:52:52,148 --> 00:52:54,317
I've been there a couple of times.

1313
00:52:54,318 --> 00:52:56,787
- You went there?
- I went with my friends.

1314
00:52:56,788 --> 00:52:58,527
- Really?
- The Botanic Park?

1315
00:52:58,528 --> 00:52:59,528
That's a sound place to visit
with your friends.

1316
00:52:59,529 --> 00:53:02,798
I thought the Botanic Park
was a place for elders.

1317
00:53:03,628 --> 00:53:05,367
- It's really nice there.
- Right.

1318
00:53:05,368 --> 00:53:06,598
Do you like plants?

1319
00:53:07,368 --> 00:53:09,497
I don't like them too much.

1320
00:53:09,498 --> 00:53:10,837
Is that so? What a bummer.

1321
00:53:10,838 --> 00:53:12,268
I'm the only one
who loves plants here.

1322
00:53:12,468 --> 00:53:13,637
I also love plants.

1323
00:53:13,638 --> 00:53:15,577
- Right.
- I have hydroponic plants.

1324
00:53:15,578 --> 00:53:16,807
- Hydroponic plants?
- They're easy to take care of.

1325
00:53:16,808 --> 00:53:18,148
- I'll teach you later.
- Hydroponic plants.

1326
00:53:18,408 --> 00:53:20,648
I have 100 times more
of what you 2 have combined.

1327
00:53:21,318 --> 00:53:24,218
I have 100 times more.

1328
00:53:24,588 --> 00:53:26,418
I've never been to the Botanic Park.

1329
00:53:27,088 --> 00:53:29,088
Don't just be working out.
Visit those places as well.

1330
00:53:29,258 --> 00:53:32,628
Right. He started out with running,

1331
00:53:32,858 --> 00:53:34,727
so I thought it was...

1332
00:53:34,728 --> 00:53:36,227
- something I would love.
- No.

1333
00:53:36,228 --> 00:53:37,668
- No!
- It ended right away.

1334
00:53:38,068 --> 00:53:40,237
I feel slightly disappointed.

1335
00:53:40,238 --> 00:53:42,337
- You should've run a bit more.
- You look like a killer right now.

1336
00:53:42,338 --> 00:53:44,338
- Really?
- Right.

1337
00:53:44,538 --> 00:53:46,267
- Okay.
- There are a lot of men here.

1338
00:53:46,268 --> 00:53:48,078
- I should hold it in.
- You look like a gunman.

1339
00:53:49,038 --> 00:53:51,548
- A ticket for 1 adult, please.
- Right. It's 5 dollars.

1340
00:53:51,948 --> 00:53:53,717
- Here you are.
- Thank you.

1341
00:53:53,718 --> 00:53:54,817
The tickets are cheap.

1342
00:53:54,818 --> 00:53:55,917
- Right.
- Right.

1343
00:53:55,918 --> 00:53:57,718
- The Botanic Park is really nice.
- Right.

1344
00:53:58,088 --> 00:53:59,918
Place the QR code here.

1345
00:54:00,288 --> 00:54:01,357
Thank you.

1346
00:54:01,358 --> 00:54:04,427
(Conservatory Entrance)

1347
00:54:04,428 --> 00:54:06,057
(He heads straight into
the Conservatory.)

1348
00:54:06,058 --> 00:54:07,528
It must feel warm in there
during the winter.

1349
00:54:09,768 --> 00:54:14,713
(Right into the warm Conservatory!)

1350
00:54:15,925 --> 00:54:17,925
(Right after entering, he heads
straight into the Conservatory.)

1351
00:54:19,595 --> 00:54:22,335
(Amazed)

1352
00:54:25,465 --> 00:54:26,604
(A place full of green
even during the winter)

1353
00:54:26,605 --> 00:54:27,965
It's really nice.

1354
00:54:28,365 --> 00:54:29,875
- It's like an amusement park.
- Right.

1355
00:54:31,175 --> 00:54:32,304
This is so fascinating.

1356
00:54:32,305 --> 00:54:34,175
I didn't know there was
a place like this in Seoul.

1357
00:54:34,645 --> 00:54:36,444
(The warm sunlight seeps in.)

1358
00:54:36,445 --> 00:54:37,575
It's warm inside.

1359
00:54:37,715 --> 00:54:40,545
(The flowers show off
their bright colors.)

1360
00:54:41,845 --> 00:54:43,154
(This place even feels mystical.)

1361
00:54:43,155 --> 00:54:44,755
It really feels mystical.

1362
00:54:45,485 --> 00:54:46,585
It looks great.

1363
00:54:47,385 --> 00:54:50,724
My hands and feet are always cold.

1364
00:54:50,725 --> 00:54:51,995
I feel cold easily...

1365
00:54:52,165 --> 00:54:53,764
and catch colds often.

1366
00:54:53,765 --> 00:54:55,565
Since I'm a singer,

1367
00:54:55,995 --> 00:54:57,864
- catching a cold...
- That would be critical.

1368
00:54:57,865 --> 00:54:59,505
- would make me lose all of my gigs.
- Right.

1369
00:54:59,735 --> 00:55:02,005
I try my best
to avoid catching colds.

1370
00:55:02,305 --> 00:55:04,335
I hate being cold.
I hate winter so much.

1371
00:55:04,905 --> 00:55:07,005
I found out that the Botanic Park...

1372
00:55:07,445 --> 00:55:09,645
was the warmest place
during the winter.

1373
00:55:09,775 --> 00:55:12,345
I wondered how warm it could be...

1374
00:55:12,745 --> 00:55:15,315
and decided to pay a visit.

1375
00:55:15,555 --> 00:55:17,754
My immune system
got weakened last year...

1376
00:55:17,755 --> 00:55:19,254
and caught colds
three times straight.

1377
00:55:19,255 --> 00:55:20,384
- Gosh.
- Gosh.

1378
00:55:20,385 --> 00:55:24,554
I've developed this obsession
of not wanting to catch a cold.

1379
00:55:24,555 --> 00:55:25,924
Isn't it worse since singers
are sensitive about their throats?

1380
00:55:25,925 --> 00:55:27,794
- What about you, Dowoon?
- I don't sing.

1381
00:55:27,795 --> 00:55:28,795
(I don't sing.)

1382
00:55:28,796 --> 00:55:29,934
I saw you sing a lot.

1383
00:55:29,935 --> 00:55:31,494
That was just
for a special occasion.

1384
00:55:31,495 --> 00:55:32,734
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1385
00:55:32,735 --> 00:55:34,565
How do you take care of your throat?

1386
00:55:34,735 --> 00:55:35,735
- It's a sensitive matter.
- As for me,

1387
00:55:35,736 --> 00:55:38,135
when I feel like
I'm about to catch a cold...

1388
00:55:38,945 --> 00:55:40,944
(How does the senior with 19 years
of experience take care of himself?)

1389
00:55:40,945 --> 00:55:42,144
I get up early...

1390
00:55:42,145 --> 00:55:43,974
and make myself sweat a lot
through a workout.

1391
00:55:43,975 --> 00:55:45,645
- That's how you catch a cold.
- Gosh.

1392
00:55:46,315 --> 00:55:47,315
(That's how you catch a cold.)

1393
00:55:47,316 --> 00:55:50,054
- That gets rid of the cold.
- You have to rest your body.

1394
00:55:50,055 --> 00:55:51,615
Have you ever missed a performance
due to a cold?

1395
00:55:51,715 --> 00:55:52,724
That has never happened to me.

1396
00:55:52,725 --> 00:55:54,155
- Really?
- Not even once.

1397
00:55:55,155 --> 00:55:58,555
I don't remember myself
catching a cold recently.

1398
00:55:59,325 --> 00:56:00,594
One's immune system
is really important.

1399
00:56:00,595 --> 00:56:01,924
The immune system
keeps you safe from colds.

1400
00:56:01,925 --> 00:56:03,094
I think good sleep is important.

1401
00:56:03,095 --> 00:56:05,165
- Right.
- Good sleep leads to that.

1402
00:56:06,765 --> 00:56:07,905
It's great in here.

1403
00:56:10,035 --> 00:56:11,035
(Breathing in)

1404
00:56:13,875 --> 00:56:14,945
(Breathing out)

1405
00:56:16,245 --> 00:56:17,645
It must feel refreshing to the nose.

1406
00:56:18,145 --> 00:56:20,215
You keep trying to smell things
in there.

1407
00:56:20,845 --> 00:56:21,885
Right.

1408
00:56:22,185 --> 00:56:23,255
It was nice.

1409
00:56:24,855 --> 00:56:27,855
It felt really warm and cozy.

1410
00:56:28,055 --> 00:56:30,055
It was damp and smelled really nice.

1411
00:56:30,825 --> 00:56:32,325
- The humidity is at 86 percent?
- Gosh.

1412
00:56:32,995 --> 00:56:35,865
Tropical plants can only live
in those conditions.

1413
00:56:36,295 --> 00:56:37,565
That's perfect for me.

1414
00:56:39,905 --> 00:56:40,965
Gosh.

1415
00:56:41,635 --> 00:56:43,574
It feels like
"Adventures of Sinbad."

1416
00:56:43,575 --> 00:56:46,145
(It feels like
"Adventures of Sinbad.")

1417
00:56:47,705 --> 00:56:50,444
(When you walk through
the thick forest...)

1418
00:56:50,445 --> 00:56:51,475
Gosh.

1419
00:56:54,315 --> 00:56:55,385
This is fascinating.

1420
00:56:56,455 --> 00:56:58,755
A palm tree is this big.

1421
00:57:02,055 --> 00:57:03,724
(He finds a huge baobab.)

1422
00:57:03,725 --> 00:57:05,094
- What?
- There's a baobab.

1423
00:57:05,095 --> 00:57:06,224
There's a baobab there?

1424
00:57:06,225 --> 00:57:07,594
(Surprised)

1425
00:57:07,595 --> 00:57:10,165
- Did you see them in Africa?
- I saw the ones there.

1426
00:57:10,465 --> 00:57:12,565
The big ones are over 30m tall.

1427
00:57:13,465 --> 00:57:15,974
(The giant trees that usually grow
in tropical climates)

1428
00:57:15,975 --> 00:57:17,275
They're unbelievably tall.

1429
00:57:17,975 --> 00:57:20,645
I heard they live
for 2,000 years to 5,000 years.

1430
00:57:21,375 --> 00:57:23,415
They have that there as well?

1431
00:57:24,615 --> 00:57:26,745
(Amazed)

1432
00:57:29,015 --> 00:57:30,015
(Breathing out)

1433
00:57:30,885 --> 00:57:31,885
(Breathing in)

1434
00:57:31,885 --> 00:57:32,885
(Breathing out)

1435
00:57:32,886 --> 00:57:33,984
- Gosh.
- Gosh.

1436
00:57:33,985 --> 00:57:34,985
(What was that?)

1437
00:57:35,255 --> 00:57:37,494
- I just wanted to smell the place.
- I thought it was Jim Carrey.

1438
00:57:37,495 --> 00:57:39,394
(I thought it was Jim Carrey.)

1439
00:57:39,395 --> 00:57:41,165
Must you smell the place
with that kind of face?

1440
00:57:41,325 --> 00:57:42,764
I get charged with freshness
by doing that.

1441
00:57:42,765 --> 00:57:44,065
- Right.
- Right.

1442
00:57:45,195 --> 00:57:47,365
(The face of wanting to feel
the most freshness)

1443
00:57:50,035 --> 00:57:51,505
(He spots a pretty flower.)

1444
00:57:52,345 --> 00:57:53,345
(Satisfied)

1445
00:57:53,775 --> 00:57:55,375
(He charges himself up again.)

1446
00:57:56,515 --> 00:57:58,744
You look like a Disney character.

1447
00:57:58,745 --> 00:57:59,945
(You look like a Disney character.)

1448
00:58:00,345 --> 00:58:02,654
Doesn't he look like a prince?

1449
00:58:02,655 --> 00:58:03,715
- Right.
- Right.

1450
00:58:06,025 --> 00:58:07,155
Gosh, it's so nice.

1451
00:58:08,825 --> 00:58:09,825
(Breathing out)

1452
00:58:12,765 --> 00:58:14,895
(The prince breathes
quite enthusiastically.)

1453
00:58:15,865 --> 00:58:19,005
(He goes around
and charges himself with freshness.)

1454
00:58:19,835 --> 00:58:21,434
(This is it.)

1455
00:58:21,435 --> 00:58:23,004
Check out his face.

1456
00:58:23,005 --> 00:58:25,744
You became a silly little boy
at the Botanic Park.

1457
00:58:25,745 --> 00:58:27,574
- I wanted to feel the place.
- I've never seen you...

1458
00:58:27,575 --> 00:58:29,345
make faces like that before.

1459
00:58:31,175 --> 00:58:33,385
(What does this smell like?)

1460
00:58:34,715 --> 00:58:35,754
(He spreads out his legs
all of a sudden.)

1461
00:58:35,755 --> 00:58:36,915
He's really into this.

1462
00:58:38,285 --> 00:58:39,655
That's how they must be felt.

1463
00:58:40,555 --> 00:58:41,984
- I always do that as well.
- Right.

1464
00:58:41,985 --> 00:58:43,955
- Right into the nose.
- Right.

1465
00:58:44,125 --> 00:58:45,155
They're just like each other.

1466
00:58:46,125 --> 00:58:47,895
(Rubbing)

1467
00:58:49,035 --> 00:58:50,494
- He really enjoys smelling them.
- He loves it there.

1468
00:58:50,495 --> 00:58:51,635
He's enjoying himself.

1469
00:58:51,965 --> 00:58:53,265
These ones are funny.

1470
00:58:54,235 --> 00:58:55,305
They really are.

1471
00:58:56,435 --> 00:58:57,974
(He's drenched in sweat.)

1472
00:58:57,975 --> 00:59:00,075
- He's drenched in sweat.
- Right.

1473
00:59:00,705 --> 00:59:02,345
Gosh, why is it so hot in here?

1474
00:59:03,175 --> 00:59:05,445
(It's too hot for me.)

1475
00:59:06,615 --> 00:59:07,814
(He heads outside
while feeling satisfied.)

1476
00:59:07,815 --> 00:59:08,845
Interesting.

1477
00:59:12,155 --> 00:59:15,325
(He puts on his jacket
right after going outside.)

1478
00:59:15,525 --> 00:59:17,154
Let's call a taxi.

1479
00:59:17,155 --> 00:59:19,124
(He calls a taxi
and heads somewhere.)

1480
00:59:19,125 --> 00:59:20,465
Where are you going now?

1481
00:59:24,335 --> 00:59:25,335
(Sighing)

1482
00:59:29,105 --> 00:59:31,235
(I feel drowsy.)

1483
00:59:32,175 --> 00:59:33,775
Why are you making so many faces?

1484
00:59:34,045 --> 00:59:35,815
You make more faces than a comedian.

1485
00:59:36,915 --> 00:59:41,585
(His facial expressions
were especially dynamic today.)

1486
00:59:42,185 --> 00:59:43,814
(Rolling his eyes)

1487
00:59:43,815 --> 00:59:45,925
I'm not sure why I was like that.

1488
00:59:48,185 --> 00:59:51,955
(He feels sleepy in the warm car.)

1489
00:59:53,525 --> 00:59:55,264
(Yawning)

1490
00:59:55,265 --> 00:59:56,795
Gosh, my mouth is so big.

1491
00:59:58,835 --> 01:00:00,565
(Yawning)

1492
01:00:01,465 --> 01:00:03,605
(His yawn has spread to him.)

1493
01:00:04,575 --> 01:00:06,574
Warm winter.

1494
01:00:06,575 --> 01:00:08,975
(Warm winter)

1495
01:00:09,575 --> 01:00:11,144
Warm.

1496
01:00:11,145 --> 01:00:13,214
(Warm)

1497
01:00:13,215 --> 01:00:16,355
I want a warm winter

1498
01:00:16,955 --> 01:00:19,425
- Warm in winter
- He has lost himself.

1499
01:00:20,785 --> 01:00:22,255
I must've gotten drunk
by the plants.

1500
01:00:23,795 --> 01:00:24,855
Gosh.

1501
01:00:25,055 --> 01:00:27,825
(He arrives somewhere
while humming.)

1502
01:00:29,065 --> 01:00:30,235
Deungchon-ro?

1503
01:00:33,135 --> 01:00:36,635
(Walking)

1504
01:00:37,335 --> 01:00:40,405
(Impressed)

1505
01:00:40,975 --> 01:00:42,105
