1757
01:10:19,649 --> 01:10:22,649
Jae Soo always carries around
a toolbox in his car.

1758
01:10:23,349 --> 01:10:24,349
Jae Soo.

1759
01:10:25,019 --> 01:10:26,849
- What are you doing?
- Nothing. I'm at home.

1760
01:10:26,989 --> 01:10:28,388
Could you come over for a second?

1761
01:10:28,389 --> 01:10:30,059
- Why?
- Help me with something.

1762
01:10:30,819 --> 01:10:31,958
What? You brought the whole thing?

1763
01:10:31,959 --> 01:10:34,458
Jae Soo is extremely talented...

1764
01:10:34,459 --> 01:10:35,528
in architecture.

1765
01:10:35,529 --> 01:10:36,859
- Really?
- Yes.

1766
01:10:37,099 --> 01:10:38,899
He also got an architectural
engineering licence...

1767
01:10:39,499 --> 01:10:41,828
in the shortest possible way.

1768
01:10:41,829 --> 01:10:42,838
Oh, my.

1769
01:10:42,839 --> 01:10:44,439
He also majored architecture
in college.

1770
01:10:44,599 --> 01:10:46,638
I knew it. The toolbox he carried...

1771
01:10:46,639 --> 01:10:48,168
seemed like an expert's.

1772
01:10:48,169 --> 01:10:49,909
- It didn't look domestic.
- Right.

1773
01:10:50,339 --> 01:10:51,938
Hold on. Let me open it first.

1774
01:10:51,939 --> 01:10:53,449
I don't know how it looks.

1775
01:10:53,509 --> 01:10:54,579
Go ahead.

1776
01:10:55,979 --> 01:10:57,018
(Rattling)

1777
01:10:57,019 --> 01:10:58,019
What does he want to do?

1778
01:10:58,020 --> 01:10:59,189
How much of it does he want to fix?

1779
01:10:59,819 --> 01:11:00,848
What do you want to do with that?

1780
01:11:00,849 --> 01:11:02,288
You want to remove it
and install a remote control?

1781
01:11:02,289 --> 01:11:03,318
- Yes.
- What?

1782
01:11:03,319 --> 01:11:04,988
So I can turn it on and off
while I'm lying.

1783
01:11:04,989 --> 01:11:06,388
Because it's cold in winter,

1784
01:11:06,389 --> 01:11:07,889
you don't want to stay
under the blanket.

1785
01:11:07,929 --> 01:11:11,658
So that I don't need to walk
to switch off the lights,

1786
01:11:11,659 --> 01:11:13,369
he and I'd install a remote control
on the ceiling...

1787
01:11:13,899 --> 01:11:16,169
and change the bulb to a warmer one.

1788
01:11:16,599 --> 01:11:18,269
My house looks a bit cold,

1789
01:11:18,369 --> 01:11:20,309
so I wanted to make it look warm.

1790
01:11:21,139 --> 01:11:23,279
(He asked for help from
the architecture genius friend.)

1791
01:11:23,479 --> 01:11:25,279
Like this. Hold it.

1792
01:11:25,879 --> 01:11:28,849
Let's see. From here...

1793
01:11:29,719 --> 01:11:32,588
I think I need to connect it
to power first.

1794
01:11:32,589 --> 01:11:34,088
You just need to install this
on the inside?

1795
01:11:34,089 --> 01:11:35,719
- Then it gets connected?
- Yes.

1796
01:11:35,959 --> 01:11:36,989
(Okay, I got it.)

1797
01:11:37,289 --> 01:11:38,358
Do you have a wire cutter?

1798
01:11:38,359 --> 01:11:39,489
I have almost everything.

1799
01:11:40,859 --> 01:11:41,928
(Jae Soo is indeed great.)

1800
01:11:41,929 --> 01:11:43,099
- There's one, right?
- Yes.

1801
01:11:44,129 --> 01:11:45,459
(Glancing)

1802
01:11:45,759 --> 01:11:46,799
Give it to me.

1803
01:11:48,369 --> 01:11:49,768
Gosh, he's so cool.

1804
01:11:49,769 --> 01:11:50,869
(He's not hesitant
as he's a genius.)

1805
01:11:51,999 --> 01:11:53,269
I'll cut it for you.

1806
01:11:55,169 --> 01:11:57,008
- Hey, punk.
- It must not be easy.

1807
01:11:57,009 --> 01:11:58,278
Even men's hearts throb
when we see it.

1808
01:11:58,279 --> 01:12:00,049
(Skillful)

1809
01:12:00,879 --> 01:12:03,019
(When the architecture genius friend
hands it over...)

1810
01:12:03,979 --> 01:12:05,248
Hey, you're good too.

1811
01:12:05,249 --> 01:12:07,119
- I know.
- I used to install ACs too.

1812
01:12:07,489 --> 01:12:09,119
Oh, right.
That's why Ji Hyeon is good.

1813
01:12:10,119 --> 01:12:11,288
(The collaboration of
an architecture genius...)

1814
01:12:11,289 --> 01:12:12,459
(and a genius
from Mokpo Technical High School)

1815
01:12:13,929 --> 01:12:15,459
(Wiping)

1816
01:12:15,759 --> 01:12:17,699
Why is it so hot here?
What's the temperature?

1817
01:12:18,159 --> 01:12:19,299
Why am I sweating so much?

1818
01:12:20,229 --> 01:12:21,599
You should lower the temperature.

1819
01:12:22,029 --> 01:12:24,139
No, I can't catch a cold.

1820
01:12:24,199 --> 01:12:25,468
Hey, that's too hot.

1821
01:12:25,469 --> 01:12:29,138
I've never seen anyone
who keeps a room hotter than mine.

1822
01:12:29,139 --> 01:12:30,338
Gosh, 30°C?

1823
01:12:30,339 --> 01:12:31,578
I keep mine at 26°C.

1824
01:12:31,579 --> 01:12:33,549
- It's at 26°C.
- Mine's at 23 or 24°C.

1825
01:12:33,649 --> 01:12:34,878
How much do you pay
for the heating bill?

1826
01:12:34,879 --> 01:12:36,078
- The heating bill...
- It must cost a lot.

1827
01:12:36,079 --> 01:12:38,678
I pay about 100 dollars more
than when I don't turn it on.

1828
01:12:38,679 --> 01:12:41,289
- Actually, I can spend that much.
- That's not too bad.

1829
01:12:41,849 --> 01:12:42,959
You've made it.

1830
01:12:43,189 --> 01:12:44,489
Of course.

1831
01:12:45,119 --> 01:12:46,929
I even got the Popularity Award.

1832
01:12:47,059 --> 01:12:48,889
Have a warm year-end.

1833
01:12:49,259 --> 01:12:50,359
It's scary what
the Popularity Award can do.

1834
01:12:50,499 --> 01:12:51,528
I can afford it.

1835
01:12:51,529 --> 01:12:52,999
(I'm warm thanks to that.)

1836
01:12:53,569 --> 01:12:55,528
Catching a cold
isn't a problem here.

1837
01:12:55,529 --> 01:12:56,569
(Even with the Popularity Award,
keeping it at 30°C is a bit...)

1838
01:12:56,669 --> 01:12:58,539
No! Don't lower it.

1839
01:12:59,509 --> 01:13:01,508
- It's hot. No, I mean, it's cold.
- Gosh, it's hot.

1840
01:13:01,509 --> 01:13:03,879
You said it's hot
without even realizing.

1841
01:13:05,679 --> 01:13:07,109
Look at you sweating.

1842
01:13:07,379 --> 01:13:08,979
It's nice to sweat and all.

1843
01:13:09,319 --> 01:13:10,778
People need to sweat.

1844
01:13:10,779 --> 01:13:12,248
(It melts)

1845
01:13:12,249 --> 01:13:13,249
And then...

1846
01:13:13,649 --> 01:13:14,919
Even the song says, "It melts."

1847
01:13:15,449 --> 01:13:16,858
Stick it in and...

1848
01:13:16,859 --> 01:13:18,319
(He's about to melt
as it's as hot as 30°C.)

1849
01:13:18,419 --> 01:13:19,828
It's done once I put it back.

1850
01:13:19,829 --> 01:13:21,188
(Ready to connect)

1851
01:13:21,189 --> 01:13:22,229
Let's give it a try.

1852
01:13:23,129 --> 01:13:25,029
All right. Let's put it back.

1853
01:13:26,029 --> 01:13:27,369
(Stepping)

1854
01:13:27,469 --> 01:13:28,929
I'll carry it for you.
Put it back in.

1855
01:13:30,069 --> 01:13:31,498
- Here.
- Yes!

1856
01:13:31,499 --> 01:13:32,969
I wouldn't have been able
to do it without you.

1857
01:13:33,839 --> 01:13:36,678
This is kind of hard to do it
by yourself...

1858
01:13:36,679 --> 01:13:38,879
because someone needs to hold it
when I put it back in.

1859
01:13:38,909 --> 01:13:40,248
- You're right.
- You need two people for it.

1860
01:13:40,249 --> 01:13:41,279
That's right.

1861
01:13:41,849 --> 01:13:43,519
(Exhaling)

1862
01:13:44,219 --> 01:13:45,219
This is it.

1863
01:13:45,220 --> 01:13:46,288
(Turning on the light again
to check)

1864
01:13:46,289 --> 01:13:47,819
(Pressing the remote control)

1865
01:13:48,649 --> 01:13:49,958
(He succeeded in connecting it
in one go.)

1866
01:13:49,959 --> 01:13:51,058
- Gosh.
- It works.

1867
01:13:51,059 --> 01:13:52,289
- It's the best.
- It's connected.

1868
01:13:52,729 --> 01:13:53,758
I told you it'd work.

1869
01:13:53,759 --> 01:13:55,159
- It was bound to work.
- Right.

1870
01:13:55,229 --> 01:13:57,058
They can be turned on
on different levels now. Look.

1871
01:13:57,059 --> 01:13:58,729
One, two.

1872
01:13:59,129 --> 01:14:00,699
I can turn it off at once
if I want to.

1873
01:14:00,869 --> 01:14:02,169
Gosh, it's so convenient.

1874
01:14:02,529 --> 01:14:03,699
It's funny, right?

1875
01:14:03,999 --> 01:14:05,138
- It's nice.
- Yes.

1876
01:14:05,139 --> 01:14:06,839
(Now, I can stay under my blanket.)

1877
01:14:06,909 --> 01:14:08,369
- So, Jae Soo,
- Yes?

1878
01:14:08,469 --> 01:14:10,778
I want to change it
to a yellow bulb.

1879
01:14:10,779 --> 01:14:11,839
A yellow bulb? Which one?

1880
01:14:12,009 --> 01:14:14,378
Look. I bought this.

1881
01:14:14,379 --> 01:14:15,379
Okay.

1882
01:14:15,449 --> 01:14:17,018
Cover... Oh, you want to
put a film over it?

1883
01:14:17,019 --> 01:14:18,118
With cellophane?

1884
01:14:18,119 --> 01:14:19,219
Really?

1885
01:14:19,449 --> 01:14:22,249
Isn't it better to leave it
and get a floor lamp instead?

1886
01:14:22,719 --> 01:14:24,959
There are times
when you need the white light bulb.

1887
01:14:24,989 --> 01:14:26,429
You can put it on and off.

1888
01:14:26,629 --> 01:14:27,958
Then you have to call Jae Soo again.

1889
01:14:27,959 --> 01:14:29,158
- Call Jae Soo again?
- No.

1890
01:14:29,159 --> 01:14:30,659
Why do you make it so inconvenient?

1891
01:14:30,999 --> 01:14:32,599
- Everyone has their lifestyle.
- Right.

1892
01:14:33,269 --> 01:14:35,029
- I'll stick this on that.
- Let's try putting it on.

1893
01:14:35,199 --> 01:14:36,399
- To see the color?
- Yes.

1894
01:14:36,499 --> 01:14:37,899
I'll turn on the light
for a second, then.

1895
01:14:39,039 --> 01:14:40,039
(Lights on)

1896
01:14:40,040 --> 01:14:41,868
- All right. Good.
- Is it okay?

1897
01:14:41,869 --> 01:14:43,139
(All right. It's warm and nice.)

1898
01:14:43,409 --> 01:14:46,049
Now, we need to stick that here.

1899
01:14:46,579 --> 01:14:48,609
- They're in different colors.
- They're all yellow.

1900
01:14:48,679 --> 01:14:49,948
Don't they need to be
in the same color?

1901
01:14:49,949 --> 01:14:51,419
They're all in different colors.

1902
01:14:52,219 --> 01:14:54,149
All right.

1903
01:14:54,819 --> 01:14:56,759
(Is this right?)

1904
01:14:57,459 --> 01:14:58,688
(Tearing the yellow cellophane)

1905
01:14:58,689 --> 01:14:59,729
All right.

1906
01:14:59,989 --> 01:15:02,559
(Sticking it on the cover
right away)

1907
01:15:03,159 --> 01:15:05,198
(Jae Soo follows
and does what Ji Hyeon wants.)

1908
01:15:05,199 --> 01:15:08,029
Jae Soo is sweating profusely.
How nice of him.

1909
01:15:08,869 --> 01:15:10,969
If you make lights like this...
This is practically a sauna.

1910
01:15:11,069 --> 01:15:12,099
It's nice.

1911
01:15:12,169 --> 01:15:14,569
During winter, people like us...

1912
01:15:15,309 --> 01:15:16,579
can't get a cold.

1913
01:15:16,679 --> 01:15:18,679
You said that for the 150th time.

1914
01:15:19,709 --> 01:15:20,849
Got it.

1915
01:15:21,149 --> 01:15:23,579
Oh, like that?
You're not covering the whole thing?

1916
01:15:23,679 --> 01:15:25,718
Yes, the color turned out well.

1917
01:15:25,719 --> 01:15:26,949
I can't wait to see the color.

1918
01:15:27,619 --> 01:15:29,359
(I hope this is going well.)

1919
01:15:29,859 --> 01:15:31,919
(Dripping)

1920
01:15:32,189 --> 01:15:33,189
I'll turn on the light.

1921
01:15:34,089 --> 01:15:35,259
(Smiling)

1922
01:15:37,759 --> 01:15:39,399
- Gosh.
- It's not bad.

1923
01:15:39,869 --> 01:15:42,268
It looks like
a modern piece of artwork.

1924
01:15:42,269 --> 01:15:43,469
It's modern art.

1925
01:15:43,639 --> 01:15:47,369
It's clearly different as this
is a group of artists.

1926
01:15:47,809 --> 01:15:49,109
- The way you think.
- Of course.

1927
01:15:50,139 --> 01:15:52,849
(The house looked cold.)

1928
01:15:53,479 --> 01:15:55,179
It looks like the lighting
of a select shop.

1929
01:15:55,609 --> 01:15:56,619
It's warm, right?

1930
01:15:57,479 --> 01:15:58,549
Nice, right?

1931
01:15:58,949 --> 01:16:00,448
(Sure. It's really warm.)

1932
01:16:00,449 --> 01:16:01,788
It's warm.

1933
01:16:01,789 --> 01:16:03,118
I got you a gift.

1934
01:16:03,119 --> 01:16:04,359
- Yes?
- Would you like to try it on?

1935
01:16:04,919 --> 01:16:06,558
(It's warm already.
What else should I put on?)

1936
01:16:06,559 --> 01:16:09,558
To keep you warm
without catching a cold...

1937
01:16:09,559 --> 01:16:11,429
Oh, the things he got
from the market earlier?

1938
01:16:12,329 --> 01:16:13,469
Are we wearing matching items?

1939
01:16:14,099 --> 01:16:15,428
Yes, they're matching.

1940
01:16:15,429 --> 01:16:17,368
Then I'll take the black one.

1941
01:16:17,369 --> 01:16:19,508
- Your fan club's color is white.
- Oh, okay.

1942
01:16:19,509 --> 01:16:20,668
Isn't this yellow?

1943
01:16:20,669 --> 01:16:21,809
It's white.

1944
01:16:22,009 --> 01:16:23,139
It's because of the lighting.

1945
01:16:23,739 --> 01:16:24,779
Because of the lighting.

1946
01:16:25,609 --> 01:16:26,879
I'll go get changed.

1947
01:16:28,979 --> 01:16:30,678
(Meanwhile,
Jae Soo puts on socks first.)

1948
01:16:30,679 --> 01:16:31,779
I should take off my hoodie.

1949
01:16:33,819 --> 01:16:35,549
Jae Soo must be really hot.

1950
01:16:37,119 --> 01:16:39,258
- Here we go, Jae Soo.
- Isn't this too much?

1951
01:16:39,259 --> 01:16:40,259
Why?

1952
01:16:40,260 --> 01:16:41,959
He's wearing fleece-lined pants
when it's already hot?

1953
01:16:42,089 --> 01:16:43,629
It's nice and warm.

1954
01:16:44,259 --> 01:16:46,028
You have to keep warm this winter.

1955
01:16:46,029 --> 01:16:47,468
- You shouldn't catch a cold.
- I think it's a bit small.

1956
01:16:47,469 --> 01:16:48,669
You shouldn't catch a cold
if you want to sing.

1957
01:16:48,999 --> 01:16:50,299
It's a project to spend winter well.

1958
01:16:50,469 --> 01:16:52,199
He's so kind.

1959
01:16:52,699 --> 01:16:53,969
It looks good on you.

1960
01:16:54,839 --> 01:16:56,379
Why do the teddy bears
look so pitiful?

1961
01:16:57,379 --> 01:16:58,679
Isn't it a life vest?

1962
01:16:59,449 --> 01:17:00,649
It's so...

1963
01:17:01,009 --> 01:17:02,819
Wear it when you're home,
so you can stay warm.

1964
01:17:03,849 --> 01:17:06,319
Oh, also... I...

1965
01:17:07,119 --> 01:17:08,789
- I need to...
- Yes?

1966
01:17:09,389 --> 01:17:11,388
The coffee table...
You have a drill, right?

1967
01:17:11,389 --> 01:17:12,688
(Taking it out)

1968
01:17:12,689 --> 01:17:14,159
- Do you know that?
- Which one?

1969
01:17:14,689 --> 01:17:16,029
A Shin-chan table?

1970
01:17:16,329 --> 01:17:17,559
- A Shin-chan table?
- Yes.

1971
01:17:17,629 --> 01:17:18,829
What's a Shin-chan table?

1972
01:17:18,929 --> 01:17:22,568
So you cover the table
with a blanket.

1973
01:17:22,569 --> 01:17:24,869
And you keep your legs warm inside.

1974
01:17:25,039 --> 01:17:26,168
Oh, a kotatsu?

1975
01:17:26,169 --> 01:17:27,639
- Oh, kotatsu?
- Kotatsu.

1976
01:17:28,169 --> 01:17:29,639
Ja Yeon has that at home.

1977
01:17:30,109 --> 01:17:31,209
That one.

1978
01:17:32,109 --> 01:17:33,978
(A Japanese-style heated table)

1979
01:17:33,979 --> 01:17:35,709
You must hate being cold.

1980
01:17:36,519 --> 01:17:38,678
Japan has a table like that...

1981
01:17:38,679 --> 01:17:40,348
because
they don't have floor heating.

1982
01:17:40,349 --> 01:17:42,218
- That's true.
- The air is cold, so...

1983
01:17:42,219 --> 01:17:43,558
Actually,
why set up a table like that...

1984
01:17:43,559 --> 01:17:44,989
in a house with floor heating
at over 30°C?

1985
01:17:45,119 --> 01:17:46,258
- Why would you even have that?
- That's...

1986
01:17:46,259 --> 01:17:47,958
- Actually, you don't need it.
- Is that so?

1987
01:17:47,959 --> 01:17:50,558
I bet it's even hotter than
the sauna you and Dowoon went to.

1988
01:17:50,559 --> 01:17:51,559
I bet so.

1989
01:17:51,560 --> 01:17:52,758
I'm using it really well.

1990
01:17:52,759 --> 01:17:54,629
Otherwise, should I put charcoal
on the inside for you?

1991
01:17:55,969 --> 01:17:56,969
(Top-notch heating)

1992
01:17:56,970 --> 01:17:58,198
Yes, put charcoal under the table
for him.

1993
01:17:58,199 --> 01:17:59,638
It'd be better to put charcoal in.

1994
01:17:59,639 --> 01:18:01,139
(You can also call me
when you need to.)

1995
01:18:01,969 --> 01:18:04,339
(Whirring)

1996
01:18:05,379 --> 01:18:07,849
(The architecture genius
performs again for his friend.)

1997
01:18:08,649 --> 01:18:09,948
It's around here, right?

1998
01:18:09,949 --> 01:18:12,578
(Skillfully disassembling
and assembling it)

1999
01:18:12,579 --> 01:18:13,888
Oh, like that?

2000
01:18:13,889 --> 01:18:15,418
Oh, you're putting it on top?

2001
01:18:15,419 --> 01:18:16,558
It fits.

2002
01:18:16,559 --> 01:18:17,959
(Just trust me.)

2003
01:18:19,319 --> 01:18:21,259
He must've wanted to
take off that vest.

2004
01:18:22,089 --> 01:18:23,598
It must've been really hot.

2005
01:18:23,599 --> 01:18:25,399
I didn't know
he was struggling that much.

2006
01:18:26,059 --> 01:18:27,668
His bangs are all wet.

2007
01:18:27,669 --> 01:18:28,929
I know.

2008
01:18:28,999 --> 01:18:31,039
